    <worksheet name='Housing Status'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Since 2023, more people arrive already homeless than at risk of becoming homeless </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' italic='true'>Clients by housing status, monthly, July 2017 - March 2026. Every client is one or the other (AIHW)</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='8' italic='true'>Until mid-2022, services generally recorded more clients at risk of homelessness than clients already homeless; short reversals during COVID did not last. The relationship changed in June 2022 and has held in every month since January 2023. By March 2026, 50,497 clients were already homeless compared with 45,949 at risk — a gap of 4,548. Over the full period, clients already homeless increased by 41%, compared with 17% for clients at risk.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='8' italic='true'>*This is an aggregate comparison of monthly client records. It does not show whether the same people moved from being at risk to becoming homeless. Data from July 2025 onward are preliminary and may be revised in future AIHW releases.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
      <repository-location derived-from='http://localhost:9100/workbooks/aihw_homeless_in_australia_review_August_2026/HousingStatus?rev=' id='132698417' path='/workbooks/aihw_homeless_in_australia_review_August_2026' revision='' />
