    <worksheet name='Indigenous Australians'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>The Indigenous-to-non-Indigenous service gap is widening everywhere, not just in remote Australia</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' italic='true'>Indigenous client rate ÷ non-Indigenous client rate, by remoteness area, 2017–18 to 2023–24. 2024–25 excluded — non-Indigenous population base not yet published (AIHW)</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' italic='true'>The Indigenous-to-non-Indigenous client ratio rose in all three areas, not only remote Australia. In major cities the ratio grew from 7.6 to 9.5, and in remote and very remote areas from 19.7 to 25.6. The remote and very remote ratio dipped once, from 24.7 in 2019–20 to 22.8 in 2020–21, before continuing upward. Rates are age-standardised, so this ratio is not an artefact of the younger age profile of the Indigenous population. </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' italic='true'>*This ratio counts people who received support, not everyone who sought it - people turned away are recorded separately as unassisted requests.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
      <repository-location derived-from='http://localhost:9100/workbooks/aihw_homeless_in_australia_review_August_2026/IndigenousAustralians?rev=' id='132698418' path='/workbooks/aihw_homeless_in_australia_review_August_2026' revision='' />
